            <div xml:id="d1697">

                <pb facs="1212" n="1096" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1096"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.93/132a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            Chinese Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 28, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Minister</hi>: Referring to previous
                    correspondence in regard to the protection of Chinese interests in Mexico, I beg
                    to inform you that the department is in receipt of two telegrams from its
                    representative at Torreon, in which he states that the defacto Government of
                    Mexico has informed him that, in matters concerning the interests of foreign
                    Governments, it desires to deal directly with accredited representatives of
                    those Governments.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
